## 2. Unified Security Severity Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`, `SR11`–`SR12`)

Security reviews use the unified 3-tier severity scale from `shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md` (never use `CRITICAL`/`HIGH`/`MEDIUM`/`LOW` or `P0`–`P3`):

| Severity | Security Finding Criteria | Impact on Sign-Off Verdict (`SR12`) |
|---|---|---|
| **`BLOCKER`** | • Authentication bypass, missing authentication on protected entrypoint, or broken session/token validation (`SR3`, `SR10`).<br>• Cross-tenant data leak / IDOR (`SR4`) or vertical privilege escalation (`SR3`).<br>• SQL/command/template injection, unsafe deserialization, path traversal, or SSRF to internal networks (`SR5`, `SR8`).<br>• Hardcoded secret, private key, credential, or raw PII leak in code, logs, or responses (`SR7`).<br>• Exploitable high-severity CVE in a reachable dependency (`SR9`). | • **`CONFIRMED BLOCKER` → `CHANGES_REQUESTED`**<br>• **`PLAUSIBLE BLOCKER` → `BLOCKED`** (until disproving/confirming evidence is supplied) |
| **`MAJOR`** | • Missing mass-assignment protection (`extra="forbid"`), unbounded pagination/upload size, or missing rate/connection caps enabling resource exhaustion (`SR5`, `SR8`).<br>• Missing `Origin` check on cookie-authenticated WebSocket, or long-lived token passed in URL query string (`SR6`, `SR10`).<br>• Missing outbound HTTP timeout, overly broad CORS, or incomplete audit logging on sensitive state transitions (`SR2`, `SR8`).<br>• Authorization matrix cell missing automated test coverage on a deep-risk path (`SR3`). | • **`CONFIRMED MAJOR` → `CHANGES_REQUESTED`**<br>• **`PLAUSIBLE MAJOR` → `BLOCKED`** (until evidence is supplied) |
| **`MINOR`** | • Defense-in-depth hardening gap with no direct exploit path (e.g., redundant security header tuning when upstream proxy already sets it, minor log-redaction improvement on non-sensitive fields). | • **`APPROVED`** (findings listed for follow-up or quick polish) |

