## 3. Redacted Security Review Report Template (`SR13`, `SR14`)

Write the security review report to `{{report_location}}` and share only via {{disclosure_channel}}. **Never paste raw secret values, tokens, or real PII into the report** — cite `file:line` and variable names only:

```markdown
# Security Review Report — <work-item> @ <revision-sha>

- **Execution Mode**: {{security_mode}}
- **Triggers Matched**: <list of matched triggers from 01>
- **Threat Model Summary**: <Assets, Actors, Entrypoints, Trust Boundaries, STRIDE risks>
- **Coverage Ledger (`SR1`)**: <N/N units COVERED, 0 UNCOVERED>
- **Authorization Matrix Coverage (`SR3`)**: <N/N cells verified>
- **CLI Gates Run**:
  - G1 Injection Scan: `PASS` | `FAIL`
  - G2 Secret Scan: `PASS` | `FAIL`
  - G3 Dependency Audit: `PASS` | `FAIL`
  - G4 Auth & Scope Test Suite: `PASS` | `FAIL`
- **Confirmed & Plausible Findings (`SR11`)**: <table of SEC-NN findings sorted BLOCKER → MAJOR → MINOR, or "0 findings">
- **Disproved / Rejected Candidates (`REJECTED`, `SR11`)**: <1-line per candidate disproved during Source→Guard→Sink trace, citing the protecting guard at file:line>
- **QA/QC Runtime Verification Hand-Off (`SR14`)**: <permission matrix rows or runtime-dependent PLAUSIBLE checks for QA/QC to execute on the live test environment>
- **Security Sign-Off Verdict (`SR12`)**: `APPROVED` | `CHANGES_REQUESTED` | `BLOCKED`
- **Prevention Rule Proposals (`SR14`)**: <new pattern/check to add to {{secure_coding_link}}, if any>
```

See [`references/01-triggers-threat-model-and-auth-matrix.md`]({{ref_01}}) for threat modeling and the authorization matrix, and [`references/02-security-checks-and-cli-gates.md`]({{ref_02}}) for boundary security checks and CLI gates.
